  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🤔 Why Authentication?\n",
    "\n",
    "### Without Authentication:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "❌ Problems:\n",
    "- Anyone can use your API\n",
    "- No usage tracking\n",
    "- No cost control\n",
    "- Abuse and spam\n",
    "- Security vulnerabilities\n",
    "- Can't identify users\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### With Authentication:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "✅ Benefits:\n",
    "- Control access\n",
    "- Track usage per user\n",
    "- Bill customers\n",
    "- Prevent abuse\n",
    "- Audit logs\n",
    "- Rate limiting per user\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Authentication Methods:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Method | Use Case | Security | Complexity |\n",
    "|--------|----------|----------|------------|\n",
    "| **API Keys** | Simple APIs, M2M | ⭐⭐⭐ | Low |\n",
    "| **JWT** | Stateless auth | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Medium |\n",
    "| **OAuth2** | Third-party apps | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | High |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔑 API Key Authentication"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from fastapi import FastAPI, Security, HTTPException, status\n",
    "from fastapi.security import APIKeyHeader\n",
    "from typing import Dict\n",
    "import secrets\n",
    "\n",
    "app = FastAPI(title=\"API Key Authentication\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# API key header\n",
    "api_key_header = APIKeyHeader(name=\"X-API-Key\", auto_error=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mock database of API keys\n",
    "VALID_API_KEYS = {\n",
    "    \"sk_test_abc123\": {\n",
    "        \"user_id\": \"user_1\",\n",
    "        \"name\": \"Test User\",\n",
    "        \"plan\": \"free\",\n",
    "        \"rate_limit\": 100\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"sk_live_xyz789\": {\n",
    "        \"user_id\": \"user_2\",\n",
    "        \"name\": \"Pro User\",\n",
    "        \"plan\": \"pro\",\n",
    "        \"rate_limit\": 1000\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "def generate_api_key() -> str:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Generate secure API key.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return f\"sk_{'test' if os.getenv('ENV') != 'prod' else 'live'}_{secrets.token_urlsafe(32)}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "async def verify_api_key(api_key: str = Security(api_key_header)) -> Dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Verify API key and return user info.\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if not api_key:\n",
    "        raise HTTPException(\n",
    "            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n",
    "            detail=\"API key required\",\n",
    "            headers={\"WWW-Authenticate\": \"ApiKey\"}\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Check if key exists\n",
    "    user_info = VALID_API_KEYS.get(api_key)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if not user_info:\n",
    "        raise HTTPException(\n",
    "            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n",
    "            detail=\"Invalid API key\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return user_info\n",
    "\n",
    "@app.get(\"/api/protected\")\n",
    "async def protected_route(user: Dict = Depends(verify_api_key)):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Protected endpoint requiring API key.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"message\": \"Access granted\",\n",
    "        \"user\": user[\"name\"],\n",
    "        \"plan\": user[\"plan\"]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "@app.get(\"/api/public\")\n",
    "async def public_route():\n",
    "    \"\"\"Public endpoint, no auth required.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return {\"message\": \"Public access\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🔑 API Key Authentication\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nGenerate new key:\")\n",
    "new_key = generate_api_key()\n",
    "print(f\"  {new_key}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nUsage:\")\n",
    "print(\"  curl -H 'X-API-Key: sk_test_abc123' http://localhost:8000/api/protected\")"
   ]
  },
